157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Data Analytics involves converting raw and unprocessed information into meaningful insights that can assist in understanding trends, evaluating performance, and making better decisions. With businesses increasingly relying on data for their day-to-day operations, the ability to examine and interpret information systematically has become an important part of modern decision-making. The field combines several approaches, including spreadsheet analysis, programming-based data processing, statistical techniques, and interactive business intelligence tools.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (This report presents the work completed during a six-week Data Analyst internship with BeeSkilled, with the practical work documented across four major learning modules. The internship began with Excel-based sales analysis, followed by dataset inspection and statistical analysis using Python and Pandas. The third module focused on data cleaning and transformation, while the final module involved an end-to-end business analytics project incorporating data validation, exploratory analysis, KPI calculation, Power BI measures, and business recommendations. Overall, the internship provided practical exposure to the process of taking raw data through different stages of preparation and analysis and ultimately converting it into useful, decision-oriented information.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (A reliable analysis begins with preparing the underlying data. Datasets obtained from practical sources may contain incomplete entries, repeated records, inconsistent formats, or values stored in unsuitable formats. Identifying and resolving such issues is therefore an essential part of the analytical process, as the quality of the input data directly influences the accuracy of the results. After preparation, the data can be examined and transformed using tools such as Microsoft Excel, Python and Pandas, and Power BI. These technologies make it possible to perform calculations, explore datasets, generate business metrics, and present analytical results through visual dashboards.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
